  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.45,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["T6", "T1"],
      "pins": ["T6.1", "T6.2", "T6.3", "T1.1", "T1.2", "T1.3"],
      "nets": ["ATO_VALVE"],
      "observed": "In the 'Main Pump & Valve Drivers' sheet the ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch is drawn as an AO3400A (small SOT-23 N-MOSFET, T6), while the AON6407 8-DFN N-MOSFET named by the spec for that position instead appears as T1 in the 24 V input path ('Reverse polarity protection'). The two N-channel devices are effectively swapped between the two positions.",
      "expected": "Specification §2 states the ATO valve switch is 'T3 — AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) | ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch', i.e. the large AON6407 should sit at the ATO valve, not a small AO3400A.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Main Pump & Valve Drivers sheet, ATO Valve block: 'T6 AO3400A'; Power Train block: 'T1 AON6407' (reverse polarity protection)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "T3 — AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) | ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch"}
      ],
      "impact": "The ATO valve is switched by a different, much smaller device than intended (lower current/thermal margin, different footprint), and the 24 V input path uses a device not described in the intended design, so the built board does not match the intended actuator drive.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    },
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["PR4", "H11"],
      "pins": ["PR4.2", "PR4.3", "PR4.4", "PR4.5"],
      "nets": ["NET0025", "NET0055"],
      "observed": "The 'WATER LEVEL SENSOR/SWITCHES' sheet contains a LiDAR module (PR4, 'LiDAR', PB_1.25mm) whose SCL/SDA/VCC/GND are wired out through H11 and tied to the main I2C bus (NET0025 / NET0055). This is the water-height sensing block.",
      "expected": "Specification §4.3/§6 states the TF-Luna LiDAR (PR1) is present in the BOM but 'its pins are typed free', 'on_board: no', i.e. it 'is not connected to any net in this design'; water level in the intended design is sensed by an HC-SR04-style ultrasonic sensor on two GPIOs, not by a wired LiDAR.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Water Level Sensor/Switches sheet, Water Height Sensor block: 'PR4 LiDAR', 'H11 PB_1.25mm', 'C53 100u', labels NET0025 / NET0055"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "the r2 netlist shows PR1 with on_board: no, in_bom: yes, and all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net in this design"}
      ],
      "impact": "The LiDAR interface is actually wired in this build (contradicting the intended design in which it is documentation-only), so the board's water-level interface differs from the specified one.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing is largely consistent with the specification, but two deviations are visible: the ATO-valve MOSFET is an AO3400A rather than the specified AON6407 (the AON6407 being used instead at T1 in the 24 V input path), and the water-level block wires a LiDAR module to the I2C bus even though the intended design leaves the TF-Luna unwired."
}

